Subject: [PATCH] v4l2_codec2: own the CSD bytes and clear the run at the session boundary

Follow-up hardening of 0017, from the reviewer's 3C audit.

1) Ownership. mCsdRun held a borrowed C2ConstLinearBlock. That pins the ALLOCATION but not
   the CONTENTS: in MediaCodec array mode the same block is handed back to the client and
   rewritten as soon as work->input.buffers is released, and V4L2Decoder only reads the bytes
   at QBUF time, i.e. during the replay. Safe on the clear-AVC path we test, unsafe in
   general (DRM / getInputBuffers). Now the CSD bytes are copied into owned storage and the
   replay blocks are rebuilt from a pool the component owns.
2) Session boundary. stopTask()/releaseTask() did not clear the run, so a stop taken after
   CSD but before the first frame left the run OPEN and the next session's SPS was appended
   to the previous run instead of replacing it. Cleared there now -- and never on a flush.
3) flushTask() no longer clears the open flag: a flush landing between csd-0 and csd-1 used
   to make csd-1 start a fresh run and drop the SPS, which is the original defect again.

